# A name that is not bound anywhere.
#
# Under `--typecheck` the type checker replaces the name analysis, so it
# is the one that catches this -- and it says exactly what the analysis
# would have said, in the same words and with the same `Name error`
# heading, because a program should be told the same thing about a name
# whichever pass noticed. Compiling the same file *without*
# `--typecheck` reports this identically.
#
# This program is expected to FAIL type checking. Its `.out` holds the
# error message, not a program's output.

count = 13
total = count + missing
